  "notes": "{制定|せいてい} refers specifically to the formal creation and enactment of laws, regulations, standards, or official rules.\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed only for legal/regulatory matters. Not for general \"creation\" or \"establishment\" of organizations or businesses.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {法律|ほうりつ}を{制定|せいてい}する: to enact a law\n- {制度|せいど}を{制定|せいてい}する: to establish a system/framework\n- {基準|きじゅん}を{制定|せいてい}する: to set standards\n- {条例|じょうれい}が{制定|せいてい}される: an ordinance is enacted\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{制定|せいてい}している means a law or rule is currently in effect (resulting state), not that someone is in the process of enacting it.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {設立|せつりつ}: establishment (of organizations, companies)\n- {創設|そうせつ}: founding, creation (of institutions)\n- {策定|さくてい}: formulation (of plans, policies — often a step before {制定|せいてい})",
